 cooler than 81% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>57\u00b0F</strong> was the 23rd coolest November 13 high (tied) of 122 since 1902, the coolest since 2022. The normal high for the date is 65\u00b0F, and the record is 83\u00b0F (1931). The low of <strong>39\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Athens has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Athens' climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Athens has set <strong class=\"sig\">38 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 78 that chance alone would give, and <strong>81 record highs</strong>, close to the 79 that chance alone would give. The 1920s hold the most record highs of any decade (75). Athens' all-time high is 109\u00b0F, on June 29, 2012.","t_chg":"Athens has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 116 complete years: Athens' average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.12\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.06 to +0.18), about +1.5\u00b0F since 1903. Athens' average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.16\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.07 to +0.25), about +1.9\u00b0F since 1903.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 5 of 12 months. Highs rose in 6 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Athens' yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.10 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 48.9 inches a year. The wettest year was 1964 (71.39 in); the driest, 1954 (28.61 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}